# Quiet the stock ZTE camera HAL's full system-property enumeration.
#
# At init the stock camera HAL walks the entire property area and reads every
# *_prop (hypervisor_*, dalvik_*, device_config_*, ctl_*, system_*, ...) — ~400
# distinct PLAT property types. This is the single largest source of AVC denials
# on a permissive boot. ZTE's downstream system policy granted these; LineageOS's
# system policy (same sepolicy version, 202504) does not — so it's a content
# divergence, NOT a version mismatch (both plat and vendor are 202504).
#
# The HAL does not functionally need these props — its own config lives in
# vendor_property_type, which the stock vendor policy already grants. So silence
# the enumeration noise rather than granting a camera HAL read of every property
# (which would be needlessly broad). dontaudit only suppresses logging; under
# enforcing the unused reads stay denied, which is correct.
dontaudit hal_camera_default property_type:file { read getattr open map };
